## Context

Author, 2026-09-06: "SDT ca dit rien, 'Index 43%' on comprend" -- SDT means
nothing to a reader, "Index 43%" is immediately understood. Ticket 0686
already asked for "human-readable states" and to "move technical
diagnostics below primary progress information"; this ticket supplies the
actual wording 0686 should adopt, so the two are not solved twice with
different vocabularies.

## Vocabulary

| Internal | User-facing (en) | fr |
|---|---|---|
| SDT pack sitter | Index assistant | Assistant d'indexation |
| SDT pack | index (of a document) | index (du document) |
| coverage | Index 43 % | Index 43 % |
| native full-text index (Zotero's own) | text search index | index de recherche textuelle |
| active document | Indexing: <title> | Indexation : <titre> |
| finished with exceptions | 12 documents could not be indexed | 12 documents n'ont pas pu etre indexes |

"SDT", "pack", "processor", "fingerprint" survive only inside the
diagnostics disclosure (see 0693), where a reader has explicitly asked for
them.

One naming conflict to resolve, not just translate around: Zotero already
has its own "full-text index" panel. The sitter's object keeps the word
"index"; Zotero's older one is relabeled "text search index" and confined
to the disclosure, so the two are never both called "index" in view at
once.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Toolbar, dialog, and all user-facing prompts use only the
      user-facing column above; "SDT" does not appear outside the
      diagnostics disclosure.
- [ ] The two "index" concepts are never both visible under the same
      unqualified label in one view.
- [ ] Wording lands before 0692 (i18n) externalizes it -- do not bundle a
      wording change and a string-externalization change in one PR; they
      cannot be diffed against each other.
